  "description": "XINZEA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C46 H86 Cu6 F18 Gd3 N6 O30 3+,3(Cl1 1-),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2B (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu3B (Cu) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.187-3.871 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.40-113.15°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd3Cu6L6(OH)6(MeOH)6(H2O)6]Cl3·5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
